<DocsExample TExample="DataGridBasicExample" Title="Columns and sorting" Description="Property columns read a value from each item, format it and sort it. Select a header to change the sort." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridTemplateColumnExample" Title="Template columns and row clicks" Description="NTTemplateColumn renders any content per row. OnRowClicked reports the row the user activated." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridAppearanceExample" Title="Appearance and density" Description="Striped rows help scanning wide tables; compact density fits more rows on screen." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridPaginationExample" Title="Pagination" Description="ShowPagination splits rows into pages. QueryParameterPrefix keeps each grid's page in the URL without colliding with other grids." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridRowDetailsExample" Title="Row details" Description="RowDetailTemplate adds an expandable detail area to each row. RowKey keeps expansion stable across updates." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridQueryStateExample" Title="Keeping filters in the URL" Description="The grid writes its page and sort to the address bar without a Blazor navigation, so NavigationManager.Uri can be missing them. When the page also writes its own query string, merge the grid's QueryParameters into that URL so its page and sort are kept for Back and reload." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridProviderExample"Title="Loading data on demand" Description="ItemsProvider requests one sorted window at a time, so large or remote data sets never load all at once." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridFullHeightExample" Title="Filling a page layout" Description="FullHeight makes the grid fill a parent with a bounded height, such as a flex column or a grid area, and scroll its rows inside it. A virtualized grid drops its default 20-row height cap and loads as many rows as the space shows. Without a bounded parent, the grid stops at the viewport height." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridResponsiveExample" Title="Small screens" Description="HideBelow drops lower-priority columns under a viewport breakpoint, and row details keep their values within reach. Below 1200px, pagination shrinks to previous, a page dropdown and next, which also works on statically rendered pages; touch screens get 48px pagination and sort targets." />
<DocsExample TExample="DataGridDragScrollExample" Title="Drag to scroll" Description="When a table is wider than its grid, mouse users can drag it sideways; touch and pen pan natively. A grab cursor and fading edges show there is more to see. A drag never clicks the button, link, or row it started on, while a short press still does. DragToScroll is on by default; turn it off when users need to select cell text." />
